      <marc:subfield code="a">For 65 million years, Madagascar was lost to the world, isolated, undiscovered, and untouched by humans. Left to its own devices it became a hotbed of evolution, resulting in the greatest concentration of unique creatures anywhere on the planet. More than 80% of Madagascar&apos;s animals and plants are found nowhere else on Earth. Recognized as one of the world&apos;s most important biodiversity hotspots.</marc:subfield>
